= Solution
{parent=a}

The <complex exponential> satisfies $e^{iz}=e^{-y}(\cos x+i\sin x)$. Multiplying by $x+iy$ gives
$$
f(z)=e^{-y}\big[(x\cos x-y\sin x)+i(x\sin x+y\cos x)\big].
$$
Thus its <real part> is
$$
\boxed{\operatorname{Re}f=e^{-y}(x\cos x-y\sin x)}.
$$

= b
{parent=2}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Taking the coefficient of $i$ in the expansion from part (a), the <imaginary part> is
$$
\boxed{\operatorname{Im}f=e^{-y}(x\sin x+y\cos x)}.
$$

