Evaluate the <cross product> componentwise and use $\sin u\cos v-\sin v\cos u=\sin(u-v)$:
$$
\boxed{\mathbf F\times\mathbf G=
\big(\sin(y-z),\ \sin(z-x),\ \sin(x-y)\big)}.
$$

= b
{parent=6}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Each component of the <cross product> in part (a) is independent of the coordinate with respect to which the <divergence> differentiates it. Thus
$$
\boxed{\nabla\cdot(\mathbf F\times\mathbf G)
=\partial_x\sin(y-z)+\partial_y\sin(z-x)+\partial_z\sin(x-y)=0}.
$$

