For a <particular integral>, try $y_p=A\cos4x$. Substitution gives $(-16+9)A\cos4x=-7\cos4x$, so $A=1$. Hence
$$
\boxed{y_p=\cos4x}.
$$
The forcing frequency differs from the homogeneous frequency, so no resonant factor of $x$ is needed.

