= a
{parent=10}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=a}

Let $S$ denote singing, and $M,F$ denote male and female. Equal population counts give $P(M)=P(F)=1/2$. The <law of total probability> therefore yields
$$
\boxed{P(S)=pP(M)+qP(F)=\frac{p+q}{2}}.
$$

= b
{parent=10}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

By <Bayes' theorem>, provided $p+q>0$,
$$
\boxed{P(M\mid S)=\frac{P(S\mid M)P(M)}{P(S)}=\frac{p}{p+q}}.
$$
If $p=q=0$, singing has <probability> zero and the stated observation cannot occur in this model; that <conditional probability> is undefined.

= 11
{parent=Paper 2}
