For a Cartesian <vector field> $\mathbf F=(F_x,F_y,F_z)$, its <divergence> is
$$
\boxed{\nabla\cdot\mathbf F=\frac{\partial F_x}{\partial x}+\frac{\partial F_y}{\partial y}+\frac{\partial F_z}{\partial z}}.
$$

= ii
{parent=a}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=ii}

The Cartesian <curl> is
$$
\boxed{\nabla\times\mathbf F=
\left(\partial_yF_z-\partial_zF_y,\ \partial_zF_x-\partial_xF_z,\ \partial_xF_y-\partial_yF_x\right)}.
$$
Each component measures circulation in the <plane> perpendicular to its corresponding coordinate axis.

= b
{parent=16}
